{"cases": [{"example": {"answer": {"selected_fact_ids": ["f2"]}, "facts": [{"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "brief periods of daily seizures", "fact_id": "f1", "kind": "frequency_rate", "normalised_label": "1 per day", "raw_value": "brief periods of daily seizures", "temporality": "current", "time_window": null}, {"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "usually every 2 weeks", "fact_id": "f2", "kind": "frequency_rate", "normalised_label": "1 per 2 week", "raw_value": "usually every 2 weeks", "temporality": "current", "time_window": null}]}, "instruction": "If one fact is unknown, 1 per day, or multiple per day during short or occasional daily spells, and another fact gives the usual gap between seizures, prefer that usual gap.", "title": "Usual gap"}, {"example": {"answer": {"selected_fact_ids": ["f2"]}, "facts": [{"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "4 seizures so far this year", "fact_id": "f1", "kind": "frequency_rate", "normalised_label": "4 per year", "raw_value": "4 seizures so far this year", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "this year"}, {"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "typically 1 per month", "fact_id": "f2", "kind": "frequency_rate", "normalised_label": "1 per month", "raw_value": "typically 1 per month", "temporality": "current", "time_window": null}]}, "instruction": "If one fact is how many seizures so far this year, and another fact gives the usual or typical rate, prefer the usual rate.", "title": "Usual rate, not a year total"}, {"example": {"answer": {"label": "2 per 6 month", "selected_fact_ids": ["f1", "f2"]}, "facts": [{"applies_to": "tonic-clonic seizures", "evidence": "2 tonic-clonic seizures", "fact_id": "f1", "kind": "unknown_frequency", "normalised_label": "unknown", "raw_value": "2 tonic-clonic seizures", "temporality": "current", "time_window": null}, {"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "seizure-free for 6 months before that", "fact_id": "f2", "kind": "seizure_free", "normalised_label": "seizure free for 6 month", "raw_value": "seizure-free for 6 months before that", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "6 months"}]}, "instruction": "If the facts give a recent count and how long the person had been seizure-free, write that count over that time. Do this only if no fact already has that label.", "title": "Recent seizures after a quiet spell"}, {"example": {"answer": {"label": "seizure free for multiple year", "selected_fact_ids": ["f1", "f2"]}, "facts": [{"applies_to": "non-epileptic attacks", "evidence": "these are non-epileptic attacks", "fact_id": "f1", "kind": "unknown_frequency", "normalised_label": "unknown", "raw_value": "these are non-epileptic attacks", "temporality": "current", "time_window": null}, {"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "no epileptic seizures", "fact_id": "f2", "kind": "unknown_frequency", "normalised_label": "unknown", "raw_value": "no epileptic seizures", "temporality": "current", "time_window": null}]}, "instruction": "If the current facts are attacks that are not epileptic seizures, write seizure free for multiple year.", "title": "Not epileptic seizures"}, {"example": {"answer": {"label": "9 per 3 month", "selected_fact_ids": ["f1", "f2"]}, "facts": [{"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "3 seizures in March", "fact_id": "f1", "kind": "frequency_rate", "normalised_label": "3 per month", "raw_value": "3 seizures in March", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "March"}, {"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "6 seizures in May", "fact_id": "f2", "kind": "frequency_rate", "normalised_label": "6 per month", "raw_value": "6 seizures in May", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "May"}]}, "instruction": "Quotes name how many seizures happened in named months, such as 3 in March and 6 in May. Add those counts and write the total over that time. Use this instead of the last month alone, unknown, or a short or vague seizure-free label. Do not replace a rate per day or per week. Do not replace seizure-free for 4 months or longer, or for any number of years. You may replace a vague seizure free for multiple label.", "title": "Month counts"}, {"example": {"answer": {"label": "2 per 2 month", "selected_fact_ids": ["f1", "f2"]}, "facts": [{"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "a seizure in March 2019", "fact_id": "f1", "kind": "unknown_frequency", "normalised_label": "unknown", "raw_value": "a seizure in March 2019", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "March 2019"}, {"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "a seizure in May 2019", "fact_id": "f2", "kind": "unknown_frequency", "normalised_label": "unknown", "raw_value": "a seizure in May 2019", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "May 2019"}]}, "instruction": "Two or more facts name seizures on different dates or months, or a quote already says how many seizures happened in a number of months. Write that count over that time. Use this instead of unknown, seizure-free after the last date, or a monthly or yearly rate when that time is more than 1 month. Do not replace a rate per day or per week. Do this only if the last dated fact looks current or recent. Ignore dates described as before an improvement.", "title": "Dated seizures"}, {"example": {"answer": {"label": "3 per 6 month", "selected_fact_ids": ["f1", "f2"]}, "facts": [{"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "3 seizures shortly after the dose change", "fact_id": "f1", "kind": "frequency_rate", "normalised_label": "3 per week", "raw_value": "3 seizures shortly after the dose change", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "following week"}, {"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "no further seizures since then", "fact_id": "f2", "kind": "seizure_free", "normalised_label": "seizure free for 6 month", "raw_value": "no further seizures since then", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "6 months"}]}, "instruction": "If the quotes describe seizures soon after a treatment change, then no further seizures for a stated time, write that burst count over the quiet time. Do this only if the quotes already give both the burst and the quiet time.", "title": "Burst after a change"}, {"example": {"answer": {"label": "1 per month", "selected_fact_ids": ["f1", "f2"]}, "facts": [{"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "last seizure on 12 March", "fact_id": "f1", "kind": "last_event_only", "normalised_label": "unknown", "raw_value": "last seizure on 12 March", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "12 March"}, {"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "remained well since then", "fact_id": "f2", "kind": "seizure_free", "normalised_label": "seizure free for 3 week", "raw_value": "remained well since then", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "3 weeks"}]}, "instruction": "If a quote names the last seizure on a calendar day, or a burst count, and says the person has been well since then, and the quiet spell is less than 6 months, write that count over that time.", "title": "Short quiet spell after a last seizure"}, {"example": {"answer": {"selected_fact_ids": ["f3"]}, "facts": [{"applies_to": "focal seizures", "evidence": "4 focal seizures this month", "fact_id": "f1", "kind": "frequency_rate", "normalised_label": "4 per month", "raw_value": "4 focal seizures this month", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "this month"}, {"applies_to": "tonic-clonic seizures", "evidence": "2 tonic-clonic seizures this month", "fact_id": "f2", "kind": "frequency_rate", "normalised_label": "2 per month", "raw_value": "2 tonic-clonic seizures this month", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "this month"}, {"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "6 seizures this month in total", "fact_id": "f3", "kind": "frequency_rate", "normalised_label": "6 per month", "raw_value": "6 seizures this month in total", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "this month"}]}, "instruction": "If several seizure types are listed, choose the highest current or recent overall count, not a breakdown by type.", "title": "Overall count"}, {"example": {"answer": {"selected_fact_ids": ["f2"]}, "facts": [{"applies_to": "seizures", "evidence": "seizure free for 2 months", "fact_id": "f1", "kind": "seizure_free", "normalised_label": "seizure free for 2 month", "raw_value": "seizure free for 2 months", "temporality": "current", "time_window": "2 months"}, {"applies_to": "absences", "evidence": "absences continue weekly", "fact_id": "f2", "kind": "frequency_rate", "normalised_label": "1 per week", "raw_value": "absences continue weekly", "temporality": "current", "time_window": null}]}, "instruction": "Do not choose seizure-free if other current seizure-like attacks are still happening.", "title": "Do not choose seizure-free while seizures continue"}], "instructions": ["Read the full clinical note and extract every seizure-frequency fact.", "For each fact, distinguish the original wording from its normalized label. Write answer.label using only the allowed forms. Copy an example and change the numbers if needed. Consider facts even when their label is unknown.", "Return only the fields defined in the supplied output schema.", "Use no seizure frequency reference only when the note contains no usable seizure-frequency evidence. Write answer.label as no seizure frequency reference and answer.evidence as null. Do not use this state when seizures are discussed but frequency is unclear; use unknown instead.", "Keep seizure-free statements separate from unknown or last-seizure-only statements.", "When the note says a last seizure occurred on a date and the patient has been well, stable, or seizure-free since, still extract the dated last-seizure fact as its own fact even if the selection is seizure-free.", "When the note says a count such as 3 or 4 jerks occurred since a dated last tonic-clonic seizure, keep that count and the date in the fact list.", "Every evidence value must be an exact substring from the note when possible.", "Return exactly one JSON object with no markdown.", "Use the cases below to decide the patient's current seizure frequency pattern. If a case matches, follow it. Write a new seizure-frequency label only when no single fact is the answer."], "label_forms": {"forms": [{"description": "A single count in one day, week, month, or year.", "examples": ["1 per day", "4 per week", "3 per month", "2 per year"], "form": "N per unit"}, {"description": "A single count over a stated number of days, weeks, months, or years.", "examples": ["1 per 2 day", "1 per 2 week", "2 per 6 months"], "form": "N per N unit"}, {"description": "A single count over a range of days, weeks, months, or years.", "examples": ["1 per 2 to 3 days", "1 per 2 to 3 weeks", "1 per 4 to 6 months"], "form": "N per N to N unit"}, {"description": "A count range in one day, week, month, or year.", "examples": ["2 to 3 per day", "2 to 4 per week", "3 to 5 per month", "2 to 4 per year"], "form": "N to N per unit"}, {"description": "A count range over a stated number of days, weeks, months, or years.", "examples": ["2 to 4 per 3 months", "2 to 3 per 2 weeks"], "form": "N to N per N unit"}, {"description": "More than one seizure in one day, week, or month, with no number given.", "examples": ["multiple per day", "multiple per week", "multiple per month"], "form": "multiple per unit"}, {"description": "More than one seizure over a stated number of months, with no number given.", "examples": ["multiple per 2 months"], "form": "multiple per N unit"}, {"description": "A count over an unstated number of days or months.", "examples": ["1 per multiple days", "1 per multiple months"], "form": "N per multiple unit"}, {"description": "How often clusters happen, and how many seizures are in each cluster. The cluster count or the time between clusters may be a range.", "examples": ["1 cluster per day, 5 per cluster", "1 cluster per week, 4 per cluster", "1 cluster per 4 months, 5 per cluster", "6 cluster per month, 4 per cluster", "1 cluster per 4 to 5 days, 2 per cluster"], "form": "cluster per unit, N per cluster"}, {"description": "How often clusters happen, and a range of seizures in each cluster.", "examples": ["1 cluster per day, 2 to 4 per cluster", "1 cluster per week, 3 to 6 per cluster", "1 cluster per month, 4 to 6 per cluster"], "form": "cluster per unit, range per cluster"}, {"description": "How often clusters happen, and more than one seizure in each cluster with no number given.", "examples": ["1 cluster per day, multiple per cluster", "1 cluster per week, multiple per cluster", "1 cluster per month, multiple per cluster"], "form": "cluster per unit, multiple per cluster"}, {"description": "Clusters are described, but how often they happen is not known.", "examples": ["unknown, 5 per cluster", "unknown, 2 to 4 per cluster", "unknown, multiple per cluster"], "form": "unknown cluster count"}, {"description": "No seizures for a stated length of time.", "examples": ["seizure free for 6 months", "seizure free for 3 months", "seizure free for 2 to 3 months"], "form": "seizure free for a duration"}, {"description": "No seizures for an unstated length of time.", "examples": ["seizure free for multiple months", "seizure free for multiple years"], "form": "seizure free for a vague duration"}, {"description": "Seizures are discussed, but there is no usable frequency.", "examples": ["unknown"], "form": "unknown"}, {"description": "There is no usable frequency evidence.", "examples": ["no seizure frequency reference"], "form": "no seizure frequency reference"}], "rules": ["Write the label using only the forms below. Copy an example and change the numbers if needed.", "Use digits, not word numbers.", "Use day, week, month, or year. Prefer the singular word.", "A night count is a day count: once per night becomes 1 per day.", "Write an upper or lower limit as that number: at most four per day, or ≤ four per day, becomes 4 per day.", "Do not write <=, >=, up to, at most, several, handful, frequent, or a calendar date.", "If none of these forms fit, write unknown when seizures are discussed, or no seizure frequency reference when there is no usable frequency evidence."]}, "note_text": "<NOTE_TEXT>", "output_schema": {"$defs": {"Answer": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"evidence": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Evidence"}, "label": {"title": "Label", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["label", "evidence"], "title": "Answer", "type": "object"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"answer": {"$ref": "#/$defs/Answer"}}, "required": ["answer"], "title": "Simple", "type": "object"}, "schema_instructions": ["The cases show intermediate facts and selections, not the response schema. Their raw_value/evidence preserve source wording; normalised_label illustrates label conversion. Populate answer.label with the case's answer label, or the selected fact's normalised_label when no new label is given. Always declare the answer label, including unknown and no seizure frequency reference, and copy its supporting quotation into answer.evidence. Only no-reference has null evidence.", "Source measurements preserve what was stated; the original cases govern the final answer, including combining counts and interpreting time. An answer conversion must not overwrite source measurements.", "Use all relevant facts and the same cases to decide the answer. Return only answer.label and answer.evidence. The intermediate facts in the cases are decision examples, not additional fields to return."], "task": "Read the clinical note. Extract every seizure-frequency fact, then select how often seizures are happening now."}

Respond with the corresponding output fields, starting with the field `[[ ## structured_json ## ]]`, and then ending with the marker for `[[ ## completed ## ]]`.
